{
 "metadata": {
  "note": "Verbatim DDInter 2.0 slice for issue #268's CLASS arm — real shipped rows, unedited. All four of Levofloxacin, Omeprazole, Esomeprazole and Amoxicillin publish `amoxicillin / esomeprazole / levofloxacin combination kit` among their own names, so a patient recorded allergic to that kit reaches all four substances — but the kit does not NAME Omeprazole: the KB reaches that row only because it publishes `esomeprazole` as its rxnorm_name, which is issue #196's borrowed-alias shape and the reason the two proton-pump rows share one ATC code. Lansoprazole is the class partner: A02BC like both of them, and not implied by the kit, so it is the subject the class arm reports a cross-reactivity FOR. The arm walks the implied substances in order and stops at the first sharing the class, which is Omeprazole — the one the record does not name — so this is where the class sentence used to assert an allergy to a drug the chart never mentions, beside an identity chip that had just declined to."
 },
